    "q-105037": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105037",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Which statement is **not** true?",
      "worked_solution": "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $R⊆Q$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every real number is a rational number. For example, we have $\\sqrt{2}\\in R$ but $\\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
