      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Which statement is **not** true?",
      "worked_solution": "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $Z⊆N$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every integer is a natural number. For example, we have $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin N.$",
