      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Which statement is **not** true?",
      "worked_solution": "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $C⊆Z$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every complex is an integer number. For example, we have $2\\text{i}\\in C$ but $2\\text{i}\\notin Z.$",
