    "q-37267": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37267",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A=\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,…\\}$ and $B=\\{5n∣n\\in N,3\\le n\\le 7\\}?$\n\nI. $B⊆A$\n\nII. $A⊆B$\n\nIII. $A⊈B$\n\nIV. $A⊇B$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the set $B.$ Substituting the values $n\\in \\{3,4,5,6,7\\}$ into the formula $5n,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=3 & \\,⇒\\,5(3)=15 \\\\ n=4 & \\,⇒\\,5(4)=20 \\\\ n=5 & \\,⇒\\,5(5)=25 \\\\ n=6 & \\,⇒\\,5(6)=30 \\\\ n=7 & \\,⇒\\,5(7)=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nB=\\{15,20,25,30,35\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
